<div class="grading-toolbar"><a class="back-link" href="{{ route('admin.demo.page', 'admin-attempts') }}">@include('pages.dictionary.icon', ['name' => 'arrow-left']) Danh sách bài chờ chấm</a><div><span class="badge badge-amber">ĐANG CHẤM · 04 / 12</span><button class="button button-quiet">Lưu nháp</button><button class="button button-primary">Hoàn tất chấm</button></div></div><div class="grading-layout"><section class="panel essay-review"><div class="essay-header"><span class="avatar avatar-small">TH</span><div><b>Trần Thu Hà</b><small>IELTS Writing Task 2 · Submitted 12/06/2024</small></div><span class="badge badge-blue">286 từ</span></div><div class="essay-question"><span class="eyebrow">ĐỀ BÀI</span><p>Some people believe that digital technology has made education more accessible. To what extent do you agree or disagree?</p></div><article class="essay-content"><p>In recent years, digital technology has changed the way people learn. I strongly agree that it has made education more accessible because learners can study from anywhere and access a wide range of learning materials.</p><p>Firstly, online courses allow students who live in remote areas to receive lessons from qualified teachers. They do not need to travel long distances or move to another city. For example, many universities now offer online programmes that can be accessed by anyone with an internet connection.</p><p>Secondly, digital libraries and educational platforms provide a great number of resources at a low cost. This helps people who cannot afford expensive textbooks or private lessons to continue their studies.</p><p>In conclusion, technology has made learning more flexible and affordable. Although access to the internet is still a challenge in some regions, the advantages are significant.</p></article><div class="feedback-area"><label>Nhận xét cho học viên<textarea placeholder="Viết nhận xét tổng quan..."></textarea></label><label class="check-line"><input type="checkbox" checked> Gửi nhận xét sau khi hoàn tất</label></div></section><aside class="panel rubric-panel"><span class="eyebrow">IELTS WRITING TASK 2</span><h3>Chấm theo rubric</h3><p>Đánh giá từng tiêu chí từ band 0–9.</p>@foreach ([['Task Response','7.0','Trả lời đúng trọng tâm, quan điểm rõ.'],['Coherence & Cohesion','7.0','Ý được sắp xếp logic, liên kết tốt.'],['Lexical Resource','6.5','Từ vựng phù hợp, còn lặp một số từ.'],['Grammar Range','7.0','Có câu phức, lỗi ngữ pháp không ảnh hưởng.']] as [$criterion,$score,$hint])<div class="rubric-score"><div><b>{{ $criterion }}</b><span>@include('pages.dictionary.icon', ['name' => 'info'])</span></div><select><option>{{ $score }}</option><option>6.0</option><option>6.5</option><option>7.5</option><option>8.0</option></select><small>{{ $hint }}</small></div>@endforeach<div class="band-result"><span>Overall band</span><b>7.0</b></div><button class="button button-primary button-full">Lưu và gửi kết quả</button></aside></div>
